{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nThe user is asking me to implement a `solve(case)` function for a grammar-guided node reduction task. Let me analyze the problem carefully.\n\nFrom the fixtures and description:\n1. We have a parse tree with nodes having: id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility\n2. We need to reduce the tree by removing nodes while:\n   - Never removing root\n   - Never removing a required symbol node\n   - Never removing a node with retained children\n   - Ensuring all required symbols remain represented after any removal\n   - Considering deeper nodes before shallower ones\n   - Using node ID as stable tie-break at equal depth\n\nThe task says \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes\" - so we process in descending depth order, and among same depth, use node ID as tiebreak.\n\nLet me think about the algorithm:\n1. Build the tree structure\n2. Process nodes in order: deepest first, then by node ID (stable tiebreak)\n3. For each node (candidate for removal):\n   - Check if removable\n   - Check if it's not root\n   - Check if its symbol is not required OR if removing it still leaves required symbols covered\n   - Check if it has no retained children\n   - If all checks pass, tentatively remove it\n4. Track removal order\n5. Return retained node IDs (sorted) and removal order\n\nWait, let me re-read: \"Never remove a required symbol node\" - this means if a node's symbol is in required_symbols, it cannot be removed.\n\nActually, re-reading: \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\" - This means we check if all required symbols still have at least one node representing them after removal.\n\nSo the algorithm:\n1. Sort candidates: deepest depth first, then by node ID (lexicographic? numeric? The IDs are like \"root\", \"n1\", \"n2\", etc.)\n2. Maintain a set of currently retained nodes\n3. For each candidate in order:\n   - Skip if not removable\n   - Skip if it's root (removable=false anyway)\n   - Check: would removing this node violate required symbols coverage? (i.e., is it the last node with its symbol among retained nodes, and that symbol is required?)\n   - Check: does this node have any currently retained children? If so, skip\n   - If passes, remove it, add to removal_order\n\nWait, \"Never remove a node with retained children\" - so a node can only be removed if all its children have already been removed (or it has no children).\n\nLet me re-read the constraints:\n- Never remove the root\n- Never remove a required symbol (node whose symbol is in required_symbols)\n- Never remove a node with retained children\n- Tentatively remove only if all required symbols remain represented\n\nActually \"never remove a required symbol\" could mean: never remove a node whose symbol is in required_symbols list. OR it could mean: never remove a node if doing so would leave a required symbol unrepresented.\n\nGiven \"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\" is a separate constraint, I think \"never remove a required symbol\" means never remove a node if its own symbol is required. But that conflicts somewhat with the other rule...\n\nActually let me re-read more carefully: the required_symbols list includes \"root\" and \"s1\". The root node has symbol \"root\" and removable=false, so it's protected by both rules. Node n1 has symbol \"s1\" and removable=false. Node n4 has symbol \"s1\" and removable=true.\n\nIf we apply \"never remove a required symbol node\", then n4 (symbol s1, removable=true) cannot be removed because s1 is required. But then \"tentatively remove only if all required symbols remain represented\" would be a softer version of the same constraint... \n\nHmm, actually I think the two rules work together:\n- \"Never remove a required symbol\" = never remove a node if its symbol IS a required symbol (hard prohibition on specific nodes)\n- \"Tentatively remove only if all required symbols remain represented\" = check the global state after removal\n\nBut wait, if we never remove a node with a required symbol, then required symbols are always represented by definition... unless there are required symbols that have no non-removable nodes.\n\nActually I think the correct interpretation is: we can remove a node even if its symbol is required, as long as after removal, all required symbols are still represented by at least one remaining node. The \"never remove a required symbol\" constraint means: if the node is the LAST representative of a required symbol, don't remove it.\n\nActually rethinking - maybe \"Never remove ... a required symbol\" means nodes that are marked with a required symbol cannot be removed regardless of other considerations. Let me look at the data:\n\nIn case b-000:\n- required_symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n- Nodes with symbol \"root\": root (removable=false)\n- Nodes with symbol \"s1\": n1 (removable=false), n4 (removable=true, depth=2)\n\nIf we can never remove a node whose symbol is required, then n4 cannot be removed either.\n\nIf we apply \"tentatively remove only if all required symbols remain represented\":\n- If we try to remove n4, after removal, s1 is still represented by n1. So we CAN remove n4.\n\nI think the second interpretation is correct: the constraint is about maintaining coverage, not about individual nodes. \"Never remove a required symbol\" probably refers to the symbol itself not disappearing from the tree.\n\nLet me go with: a node can be removed if:\n1. It is removable=true\n2. It is not root (actually covered by removable=false)\n3. It has no currently retained children\n4. After removal, all required symbols still have at least one retained node representing them\n\nNow the ordering: \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes\" + \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth\"\n\nSo we sort by (-depth, node_id) to get deepest first, then by node_id for ties.\n\nNode IDs are \"root\", \"n1\", \"n2\", ... \"n6\". For lexicographic sort: n1 \u003c n2 \u003c n3 \u003c n4 \u003c n5 \u003c n6 \u003c root. That seems reasonable.\n\nLet me trace through case b-000:\n\nNodes:\n- root: depth=0, removable=false, symbol=root\n- n1: depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s1\n- n2: depth=1, removable=true, symbol=s2\n- n3: depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s0\n- n4: depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s1, parent=n2\n- n5: depth=2, removable=false, symbol=s2, parent=n3\n- n6: depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s0, parent=n1\n\nChildren map:\n- root: [n1, n2, n3]\n- n1: [n6]\n- n2: [n4]\n- n3: [n5]\n\nProcess in order (deepest first, then by ID):\nDepth 2 candidates: n4, n5, n6 (sorted by ID: n4, n5, n6)\nDepth 1 candidates: n1, n2, n3 (sorted by ID: n1, n2, n3)\nDepth 0: root\n\nStart with all nodes retained.\n\nProcess n4 (depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s1, parent=n2):\n- removable=true ✓\n- Has children? n4 has no children ✓\n- After removal, required symbols: root (root still there), s1 (n1 still there) ✓\n- Remove n4. removal_order = [n4]\n\nProcess n5 (depth=2, removable=false, symbol=s2, parent=n3):\n- removable=false ✗\n- Skip\n\nProcess n6 (depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s0, parent=n1):\n- removable=true ✓\n- Has children? n6 has no children ✓\n- After removal, required symbols covered? root: yes, s1: n1 and n4... wait n4 was removed. s1: n1 still retained ✓\n- Remove n6. removal_order = [n4, n6]\n\nProcess n1 (depth=1, removable=false):\n- removable=false ✗\n- Skip\n\nProcess n2 (depth=1, removable=true, symbol=s2, parent=root):\n- removable=true ✓\n- Has children? n4 was removed, so n2's children: n4 is removed. No retained children ✓\n- After removal, required symbols: root (yes), s1 (n1 retained) ✓\n- Remove n2. removal_order = [n4, n6, n2]\n\nProcess n3 (depth=1, removable=false):\n- removable=false ✗\n- Skip\n\nProcess root (depth=0, removable=false):\n- removable=false ✗\n- Skip\n\nFinal retained: root, n1, n3, n5\nSorted retained IDs: [\"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\", \"root\"]\nRemoval order: [\"n4\", \"n6\", \"n2\"]\n\nThat looks correct.\n\nNow let me implement this:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    payload = case[\"payload\"]\n    nodes = payload[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(payload[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Build data structures\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Current retained set\n    retained = set(n[\"id\"] for n in nodes)\n    \n    # Symbol to retained node IDs mapping\n    symbol_to_nodes = {}\n    for n in nodes:\n        sym = n[\"symbol\"]\n        if sym not in symbol_to_nodes:\n            symbol_to_nodes[sym] = set()\n        symbol_to_nodes[sym].add(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Sort candidates: deepest first, then by node ID\n    candidates = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    removal_order = []\n    \n    for node in candidates:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Must be removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Must have no retained children\n        has_retained_children = any(c in retained for c in children[nid])\n        if has_retained_children:\n            continue\n        \n        # Check: after removal, all required symbols still represented\n        sym = node[\"symbol\"]\n        if sym in required_symbols:\n            # This is the only retained node with this required symbol?\n            if len(symbol_to_nodes.get(sym, set())) \u003c= 1:\n                continue  # Can't remove, would lose required symbol\n        \n        # Remove the node\n        retained.remove(nid)\n        if sym in symbol_to_nodes:\n            symbol_to_nodes[sym].discard(nid)\n        removal_order.append(nid)\n    \n    retained_ids = sorted(retained)\n    \n    return {\n        \"retained_ids\": retained_ids,\n        \"removal_order\": removal_order\n    }\n```\n\nWait, I need to check the symbol_to_nodes tracking more carefully. Initially it contains all nodes. When we remove a node, we remove it from symbol_to_nodes. So `len(symbol_to_nodes.get(sym, set())) \u003c= 1` would be True if the current node is the only one with that required symbol still retained.\n\nLet me trace through again with case b-000:\n\nInitial symbol_to_nodes:\n- root: {root}\n- s1: {n1, n4}\n- s2: {n2, n5}\n- s0: {n3, n6}\n\nProcess n4 (symbol=s1, required):\n- symbol_to_nodes[s1] = {n1, n4}, len=2, so 2 \u003e 1, can remove\n- Remove n4, symbol_to_nodes[s1] = {n1}\n\nProcess n5 (removable=false): skip\n\nProcess n6 (symbol=s0, not required):\n- Remove n6, symbol_to_nodes[s0] = {n3}\n\nProcess n1 (removable=false): skip\n\nProcess n2 (symbol=s2, not required):\n- children: n4 (removed) → no retained children\n- Remove n2, symbol_to_nodes[s2] = {n5}\n\nProcess n3 (removable=false): skip\n\nProcess root (removable=false): skip\n\nRetained: {root, n1, n3, n5}\nSorted: [\"n1\", \"n3\", \"n5\", \"root\"]\nRemoval order: [\"n4\", \"n6\", \"n2\"]\n\nThis matches my earlier trace. The implementation looks correct.\n\nNow let me also make sure I handle the case where a node might have \"retained children\" - I use the retained set to track this, not the original node list.\n\nAlso need to validate required fields. The problem says \"Validate every required field before computing a result.\" Let me add validation.\n\nRequired fields from the payload:\n- nodes: list with each having id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility\n- required_symbols: list\n\nLet me write the final implementation with validation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    # Validate required fields\n    if \"payload\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing 'payload' in case\")\n    payload = case[\"payload\"]\n    \n    if \"nodes\" not in payload:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing 'nodes' in payload\")\n    if \"required_symbols\" not in payload:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing 'required_symbols' in payload\")\n    \n    nodes = payload[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(payload[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Validate each node\n    required_node_fields = {\"id\", \"parent\", \"symbol\", \"depth\", \"removable\", \"utility\"}\n    for n in nodes:\n        missing = required_node_fields - set(n.keys())\n        if missing:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Node missing fields: {missing}\")\n    \n    # Build data structures\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Current retained set\n    retained = set(n[\"id\"] for n in nodes)\n    \n    # Symbol to retained node IDs\n    symbol_to_retained = {}\n    for n in nodes:\n        sym = n[\"symbol\"]\n        if sym not in symbol_to_retained:\n            symbol_to_retained[sym] = set()\n        symbol_to_retained[sym].add(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Sort: deepest first, then by node ID (lexicographic)\n    candidates = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    removal_order = []\n    \n    for node in candidates:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Must be removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Must have no retained children\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\n            continue\n        \n        # If symbol is required, must not be the last retained node with that symbol\n        sym = node[\"symbol\"]\n        if sym in required_symbols and len(symbol_to_retained.get(sym, set())) \u003c= 1:\n            continue\n        \n        # Remove the node\n        retained.remove(nid)\n        symbol_to_retained[sym].discard(nid)\n        removal_order.append(nid)\n    \n    retained_ids = sorted(retained)\n    \n    return {\n        \"retained_ids\": retained_ids,\n        \"removal_order\": removal_order\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks good. The response format needs to be a JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a string.\n\nLet me write the JSON response. I need to escape the Python source properly as a JSON string (escape newlines, backslashes, quotes).\n\nThe implementation is clean and straightforward. Let me finalize it.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate required fields\\n    if \\\"payload\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing 'payload' in case\\\")\\n    payload = case[\\\"payload\\\"]\\n    if \\\"nodes\\\" not in payload:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing 'nodes' in payload\\\")\\n    if \\\"required_symbols\\\" not in payload:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing 'required_symbols' in payload\\\")\\n\\n    nodes = payload[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(payload[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    # Validate each node has required fields\\n    required_node_fields = {\\\"id\\\", \\\"parent\\\", \\\"symbol\\\", \\\"depth\\\", \\\"removable\\\", \\\"utility\\\"}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        missing = required_node_fields - set(n.keys())\\n        if missing:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Node {n.get('id', '?')} missing fields: {missing}\\\")\\n\\n    # Build children map\\n    children = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n[\\\"parent\\\"] is not None:\\n            if n[\\\"parent\\\"] not in children:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Node {n['id']} references unknown parent {n['parent']}\\\")\\n            children[n[\\\"parent\\\"]].append(n[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    # Track retained nodes and per-symbol counts of retained nodes\\n    retained = set(n[\\\"id\\\"] for n in nodes)\\n    symbol_to_retained = {}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        sym = n[\\\"symbol\\\"]\\n        if sym not in symbol_to_retained:\\n            symbol_to_retained[sym] = set()\\n        symbol_to_retained[sym].add(n[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    # Process order: deepest first; stable tie-break by node ID (lexicographic)\\n    candidates = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n\\n    removal_order = []\\n\\n    for node in candidates:\\n        nid = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n\\n        # Hard constraint: node must be marked removable\\n        if not node[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Hard constraint: no retained children\\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Hard constraint: required symbols must remain represented after removal\\n        sym = node[\\\"symbol\\\"]\\n        if sym in required_symbols and len(symbol_to_retained.get(sym, set())) \u003c= 1:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # All constraints satisfied — remove the node\\n        retained.remove(nid)\\n        symbol_to_retained[sym].discard(nid)\\n        removal_order.append(nid)\\n\\n    retained_ids = sorted(retained)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"retained_ids\\\": retained_ids,\\n        \\\"removal_order\\\": removal_order\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01ahYXsqJTiO890mRAJstIm1","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":39},"cache_creation_input_tokens":39,"cache_read_input_tokens":2037,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":41,"output_tokens":4542,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3822},"service_tier":"standard"}}